Collecting and Using Your Personal Data

Data You provide

- Account data: an account identifier and, when You sign in with email, Your email address. Sign in with Apple or Google provides the identity data those services return.
- Profile data: nutrition targets, locale, units, and the onboarding inputs You enter (such as age, height, weight, activity level, and goal).
- Nutrition data: the meal results You confirm (name, calorie estimate and range, macronutrients, ingredients, and Your corrections) and Your weight entries.
- Purchase data: Your subscription entitlement status, linked to Apple's original transaction identifier. We do not receive or store payment card details; payment is handled entirely by Apple.
- Usage metering: the date and count of AI scans, used to enforce the free daily scan limit.

Photos, voice, and text descriptions

When You choose to scan a meal, the Application creates a reduced-size copy of the photo, sends it over an encrypted connection for nutrition analysis, and deletes the temporary copy from the app cache after the request completes. Photos taken with the in-app camera are also deleted from the Device after processing. Photos are never stored in Our database or on Our servers — only the nutrition result You confirm is saved.

When You dictate meals, speech recognition on Your Device creates a text transcript that You review before it is sent for analysis. Typed descriptions work the same way. AI analysis requests are processed with Zero Data Retention routing: the provider does not store the photo, transcript, or description after answering the request.

Barcode scanning sends only the barcode number to the product database; no account information is attached.

Service Providers

We share data only with the processors needed to run the Service, and only the information needed for their function:

- Google Firebase — account authentication.
- Supabase — secure cloud storage of Your profile, nutrition, and weight data.
- OpenRouter — AI nutrition analysis with Zero Data Retention routing.
- Apple — subscription purchases and confirmation of subscription status.
- Open Food Facts — barcode and food product data (receives only the barcode number or search text).

We do not use advertising networks, analytics SDKs, or tracking technologies, and We do not sell or rent Personal Data.

Retention and Deletion

Nutrition and weight records remain until You delete them or delete Your account. Deleting Your account from inside the Application removes Your Firebase account and all connected records (profile, meals, weights, scan usage, and the entitlement link to Your App Store subscription).

Deleting Your account does not cancel an active App Store subscription; subscriptions must be cancelled separately in Your Apple settings.

Your Rights

If You are in the European Economic Area, You have the right to access, correct, export, restrict, object to the processing of, and erase Your Personal Data. Most of these rights can be exercised directly in the Application (editing or deleting entries, and full account deletion). For anything else, contact Us at the address below. You also have the right to lodge a complaint with Your local data protection authority (in the Netherlands: Autoriteit Persoonsgegevens).

Children

The Service is not directed at children under 13, and We do not knowingly collect Personal Data from children under 13. Users under 18 are always given a maintenance calorie target, never a calorie deficit.

Security

All communication between the Application and Our servers uses encrypted connections (HTTPS). Server-side data access is restricted to authenticated, user-scoped requests.

Medical Disclaimer

Nutrition results are estimates presented as ranges and are provided for informational purposes only. They are not medical advice. Consult a qualified professional before making decisions about Your health.

